{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 COLLECTION — ONE PRODUCT'S DOT RAIL and its stop states (WINNING-SPEC §4.2, §3.4).

  The ruler is the section the ruling exists for, and this snippet is the part of it that must be
  identical on every row: the product's own hairline rail, one lit dot per REAL option value positioned
  by its number, and — rendered into the DOM all at once, so CSS alone can choose between them — one
  answer per page stop.

  NOTHING HERE IS JAVASCRIPT. §3.4's no-JS contract is absolute: the stops narrow with scripting off,
  every price is already in the document and CSS picks which one shows. That is why every stop's answer
  is printed and hidden, and never fetched.

  §6.6 is absolute too: a product that cannot reach the stop DIMS AND SAYS HOW FAR IT DOES REACH.
  `display:none` on a product row is a breach. This snippet never emits one.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the three stop states (+2)
  For a page stop S (a number in the rail's unit) and a product whose axis runs min…max:

    below   S is under the product's smallest value. The product still answers — with its smallest
            offering, which OVERSHOOTS the stop. `data-state="below"`. Full price, full per-unit line.
            (decor at 3 מ׳: Edison answers 5 מ׳ — 139.90 ₪.)
    at      S is inside min…max. The answer is the value AT or IMMEDIATELY ABOVE S, and its exact
            price. `data-state="at"`. (decor at 10 מ׳: rope 12 מ׳ — 99.90 ₪, crystal 11 מ׳ — 109.90 ₪,
            globe 10 מ׳ — 169.90 ₪.)
    beyond  S is past max. The row DIMS to .4 and prints "האורך המרבי: 8 מ׳". `data-state="beyond"`.
            (decor at 10 מ׳: Edison. This is §4.2 non-negotiable 2 and §6.6.)

  and two more that are not stop states but must exist:

    span    the answer at the "הכול" stop: the product's whole range, "5–22 מ׳", with the house price
            rule (elmsnest-v2-price). This is what a visitor sees before touching anything.
    off     the product is not measured in this rail's unit at all — a colour/model axis, an axis with
            no number, or an AREA axis. The rail root gets .env2-coll-rail--off, prints no dots, and
            carries the caller's off_note. §3.4: such a product is never drawn as a span on this rail;
            it is lifted into its own band (§4.3) with a real photograph and a real card.
            decorative-led-net-lights is the reason this state exists (§4.5 non-negotiable 3).

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ call signatures
    once per page, before any rail:
      {% render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-rail', css: true %}                       the static stylesheet
      {% render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-rail', emit: 'css', stops: env2_stops,
                rail_max: env2_rail_max, scope: '.env2-coll-ruler__body' %}  the :checked ruleset

    once per product row:
      {%- capture env2_short -%}
        {%- render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-rail', product: p, stops: env2_stops, unit: 'm', emit: 'short' -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      <div class="env2-coll-ruler__row" data-short="{{ env2_short | strip }}">
        …title, axis caption…
        {% render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-rail', product: p, stops: env2_stops, unit: 'm',
                  rail_max: env2_rail_max, miss_label: 'האורך המרבי' %}
        …price column, action…
      </div>

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ inputs
    product   : required for 'rail' and 'short'. Blank -> nothing at all.
    stops     : the page's stop set, a comma list of numbers, ascending: '3,6,10,15,22,30'.
                THE KEY IS THE NUMBER WITH '.' REPLACED BY '_': the stop 6.5 keys as 6_5, because the
                CSS selector #env2-stop-6.5 reads as id 'env2-stop-6' plus class '5' and silently stops
                narrowing. Your radio ids, your labels' `for`, and the #len- hash must use the SAME
                transform: {%- assign k = stop | replace: '.', '_' -%}.
                Generated by the ruler section from the union of every product's axis (§3.4) —
                never typed. 'הכול' is implicit and always rendered; do not put it in the list.
    unit      : the rail's unit key from elmsnest-v2-coll-axis — m | qty | led | w | k.
                A product whose axis unit differs (or is 'area', or carries no number) renders 'off'.
    rail_min  : the rail's left-hand number. Default 0.
    rail_max  : the rail's right-hand number. Default = the largest stop.
    miss_label: the 'beyond' label. Default 'האורך המרבי' for m, 'הכמות המרבית' for qty,
                'המידה המרבית' otherwise. §4.2 fixes only the metre wording; the section owns the rest.
    off_note  : one line printed inside an 'off' rail — decorative-led-net-lights gets
                'נמדדת לפי שטח, לא לפי אורך' (§3.4). Blank -> nothing is printed.
    per_unit_word : override the derived per-unit noun; path prints '₪ לנקודת אור' (C2). Blank ->
                '₪ למטר' / '₪ ליחידה' from the axis snippet.
                BIDI, load-bearing: the '≈' goes INSIDE the <bdi> — <bdi>≈9.99</bdi> ₪ למטר. Left
                outside it, the RTL algorithm moves it to the far edge of the line and the page prints
                '9.99 ₪ למטר≈'. Every caller that builds its own per-unit string must do the same.
    show_per  : false to suppress the derived per-unit line (the ruler's show_unit_price setting).
    scope     : ('css' emit) the selector the generated rules are scoped under. Default
                '.env2-coll-ruler__body'. It must be a SIBLING of the radios, after them in the DOM.
    emit      : 'rail' (default) | 'short' | 'css'
    css       : true -> print ONLY the static stylesheet.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ what 'rail' prints
    <div class="env2-coll-rail" data-unit="m" data-state="on" data-short="10 15 22 30"
         style="--env2-rail-max:32">
      <span class="env2-coll-rail__line"></span>                          the hairline
      <span class="env2-coll-rail__dot" data-n="5" data-pick="all 3 6"
            style="--env2-rail-p:15.63%"></span>                          one per real option value
      …
      <span class="env2-coll-rail__v env2-coll-rail__v--all" data-stop="all" data-state="span">
        <b class="env2-coll-rail__val">5–22 מ׳</b>
        <span class="env2-coll-rail__price">…elmsnest-v2-price…</span>
      </span>
      <span class="env2-coll-rail__v" data-stop="10" data-state="at" data-n="11"
            data-variant-id="123">
        <b class="env2-coll-rail__val"><bdi>11</bdi> מ׳</b>
        <span class="env2-coll-rail__price"><bdi>109.90</bdi> ₪</span>
        <span class="env2-coll-rail__per"><bdi>≈9.99</bdi> ₪ למטר</span>
      </span>
      <span class="env2-coll-rail__v" data-stop="15" data-state="beyond">
        <span class="env2-coll-rail__miss">האורך המרבי: <bdi>13</bdi> מ׳</span>
      </span>
    </div>

    'short' prints ONLY the space-separated list of stops at which this product is 'beyond'
    ("10 15 22 30"), with no markup, so the caller can put it on the ROW and dim the whole row.
    A product with no short stop prints an empty string.
    The rail root carries the SAME data-short, so a caller who forgets still dims something honest;
    the generated ruleset resets a nested duplicate to opacity 1 so the two can never compound to .16.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ what 'css' prints
    One <style> holding, per stop N of `stops` plus 'all':
      #env2-stop-N:checked ~ SCOPE .env2-coll-rail__v{display:none}
      #env2-stop-N:checked ~ SCOPE .env2-coll-rail__v[data-stop="N"]{display:flex}
      #env2-stop-N:checked ~ SCOPE .env2-coll-rail__dot[data-pick~="N"]{…lit…}
      #env2-stop-N:checked ~ SCOPE [data-short~="N"]{opacity:.4}
      #env2-stop-N:checked ~ SCOPE [data-short~="N"] [data-short~="N"]{opacity:1}   (no compounding)
      #env2-stop-N:checked ~ SCOPE .env2-coll-rail__cursor{inset-inline-start:P%}
      #env2-stop-N:checked ~ SCOPE .env2-pill[for="env2-stop-N"]{…the lit pill…}
    The ruler section supplies the radios (name="env2-stop", ids env2-stop-all / env2-stop-3 …) BEFORE
    the scope element, and puts .env2-coll-rail__cursor on its cursor knob. That is the whole
    mechanism — it is `howmuch/index.html:229-262` and it narrows with JavaScript disabled.

  Radius note: the dots and the cursor knob are 999px. §3.1 allows exactly two round things on this
  page — pill buttons and the cursor knob — and a dot rail with square dots is not a dot rail.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_mode = emit | default: 'rail'
  if css == true
    assign env2_mode = 'css_static'
  endif
  if env2_mode == 'rail' or env2_mode == 'short'
    if product == blank
      assign env2_mode = 'none'
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if env2_mode == 'rail' or env2_mode == 'short' -%}
{%- capture env2_axis -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-coll-axis', product: product, per_unit_word: per_unit_word, emit: 'rows' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign FS = '~~F~~'
  assign RS = '~~R~~'
  assign recs = env2_axis | split: RS
  assign meta = recs[0] | split: FS
  assign a_unit = meta[3]
  assign a_measured = meta[9]
  assign a_min = meta[11]
  assign a_max = meta[12]
  assign a_maxprice = meta[13]
  assign a_label = meta[4]

  assign want = unit | default: a_unit
  assign on = false
  if a_measured == '1' and a_unit == want and a_unit != ''
    assign on = true
  endif

  assign stoplist = stops | default: '' | split: ','
  assign rmin = rail_min | default: 0 | plus: 0.0
  assign rmax = rail_max | default: 0 | plus: 0.0
  if rmax <= rmin
    assign rmax = a_max | default: 1 | plus: 0.0
    for s in stoplist
      assign sf = s | plus: 0.0
      if sf > rmax
        assign rmax = sf
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign rspan = rmax | minus: rmin
  if rspan <= 0
    assign rspan = 1.0
  endif

  assign miss = miss_label | default: ''
  if miss == ''
    if a_unit == 'm'
      assign miss = 'האורך המרבי'
    elsif a_unit == 'qty'
      assign miss = 'הכמות המרבית'
    else
      assign miss = 'המידה המרבית'
    endif
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- the answer per stop, one min-search
  # answers  = '|<stop>^<i>^<state>|…'   picks = '|<i>=<stop>|…'   shortlist = the 'beyond' stops
  assign answers = '|'
  assign picks = '|'
  assign shortlist = ''
  if on
    assign minf = a_min | plus: 0.0
    assign maxf = a_max | plus: 0.0
    for s in stoplist
      assign sf = s | plus: 0.0
      assign sk = s | replace: '.', '_'
      assign best = -1
      assign bestn = 0.0
      for rec in recs offset: 1
        assign r = rec | split: FS
        if r[3] != '' and r[4] == a_unit
          assign cand = r[3] | plus: 0.0
          if cand >= sf
            if best < 0 or cand < bestn
              assign best = r[1] | plus: 0
              assign bestn = cand
            endif
          endif
        endif
      endfor
      if best < 0
        assign shortlist = shortlist | append: ' ' | append: sk
        assign answers = answers | append: sk | append: '^^beyond|'
      else
        assign st = 'at'
        if sf < minf
          assign st = 'below'
        endif
        assign answers = answers | append: sk | append: '^' | append: best | append: '^' | append: st | append: '|'
        assign picks = picks | append: best | append: '=' | append: sk | append: '|'
      endif
    endfor
    # the 'הכול' stop answers with the smallest offering, and its dot is the lit one
    assign firstlow = -1
    assign firstlown = 0.0
    for rec in recs offset: 1
      assign r = rec | split: FS
      if r[3] != '' and r[4] == a_unit
        assign cand = r[3] | plus: 0.0
        if firstlow < 0 or cand < firstlown
          assign firstlow = r[1] | plus: 0
          assign firstlown = cand
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    if firstlow >= 0
      assign picks = picks | append: firstlow | append: '=all|'
    endif
  endif
  assign shortlist = shortlist | strip
-%}
{%- if env2_mode == 'short' -%}{{ shortlist }}{%- else -%}
{%- liquid
  assign state = 'off'
  if on
    assign state = 'on'
  endif
  assign showper = true
  if show_per == false
    assign showper = false
  endif
-%}
<div class="env2-coll-rail{% unless on %} env2-coll-rail--off{% endunless %}" data-unit="{{ want | escape }}" data-state="{{ state }}"{% if shortlist != '' %} data-short="{{ shortlist | escape }}"{% endif %} style="--env2-rail-max:{{ rmax }}">
  {%- if on -%}
    <span class="env2-coll-rail__line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    {%- for rec in recs offset: 1 -%}
      {%- assign r = rec | split: FS -%}
      {%- if r[3] != '' and r[4] == a_unit -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign dn = r[3] | plus: 0.0
          assign dp = dn | minus: rmin | times: 100.0 | divided_by: rspan | round: 2
          if dp < 0
            assign dp = 0
          endif
          if dp > 100
            assign dp = 100
          endif
          assign dkey = '|' | append: r[1] | append: '='
          assign dpick = ''
          assign pentries = picks | split: '|'
          for pe in pentries
            assign pp = pe | split: '='
            if pp.size > 1 and pp[0] == r[1]
              assign dpick = dpick | append: ' ' | append: pp[1]
            endif
          endfor
          assign dpick = dpick | strip
        -%}
        <span class="env2-coll-rail__dot" data-n="{{ r[3] }}"{% if dpick != '' %} data-pick="{{ dpick }}"{% endif %} style="--env2-rail-p:{{ dp }}%" title="{{ r[2] | escape }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    <span class="env2-coll-rail__v env2-coll-rail__v--all" data-stop="all" data-state="span">
      <b class="env2-coll-rail__val">{% if a_min == a_max %}<bdi>{{ a_min }}</bdi>{% else %}<bdi>{{ a_min }}–{{ a_max }}</bdi>{% endif %} {{ a_label }}</b>
      <span class="env2-coll-rail__price">{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-price', product: product -%}</span>
    </span>
    {%- for s in stoplist -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign sk = s | replace: '.', '_'
        assign akey = '|' | append: sk | append: '^'
        assign ahit = answers | split: akey
        assign afld = ''
        if ahit.size > 1
          assign afld = ahit[1] | split: '|' | first
        endif
        assign aparts = afld | split: '^'
        assign aidx = aparts[0]
        assign astate = aparts[1] | default: 'beyond'
        if afld == '^beyond'
          assign aidx = ''
          assign astate = 'beyond'
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if astate == 'beyond' -%}
        <span class="env2-coll-rail__v" data-stop="{{ sk }}" data-state="beyond">
          <span class="env2-coll-rail__miss">{{ miss }}: <bdi>{{ a_max }}</bdi> {{ a_label }}</span>
          <span class="env2-coll-rail__price env2-coll-rail__price--miss"><bdi>{{ a_maxprice }}</bdi> ₪</span>
        </span>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- for rec in recs offset: 1 -%}
          {%- assign r = rec | split: FS -%}
          {%- if r[1] == aidx -%}
            <span class="env2-coll-rail__v" data-stop="{{ sk }}" data-state="{{ astate }}" data-n="{{ r[3] }}" data-variant-id="{{ r[16] }}">
              <b class="env2-coll-rail__val"><bdi>{{ r[3] }}</bdi> {{ r[5] }}</b>
              <span class="env2-coll-rail__price"><bdi>{{ r[10] }}</bdi> ₪</span>
              {%- if showper and r[13] != '' -%}
                <span class="env2-coll-rail__per"><bdi>≈{{ r[13] }}</bdi> {{ r[14] }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- elsif off_note != blank -%}
    <p class="env2-coll-rail__off">{{ off_note }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if env2_mode == 'css' -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sc = scope | default: '.env2-coll-ruler__body'
  assign stoplist = stops | default: '' | split: ','
  assign rmin = rail_min | default: 0 | plus: 0.0
  assign rmax = rail_max | default: 0 | plus: 0.0
  if rmax <= rmin
    assign rmax = 1.0
    for s in stoplist
      assign sf = s | plus: 0.0
      if sf > rmax
        assign rmax = sf
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  assign rspan = rmax | minus: rmin
  if rspan <= 0
    assign rspan = 1.0
  endif
-%}
<style id="env2-coll-rail-stops">
{%- for s in stoplist -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sk = s | replace: '.', '_'
  assign cp = s | plus: 0.0 | minus: rmin | times: 100.0 | divided_by: rspan | round: 2
  if cp < 0
    assign cp = 0
  endif
  if cp > 100
    assign cp = 100
  endif
-%}
#env2-stop-{{ sk }}:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__v{display:none}
#env2-stop-{{ sk }}:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__v[data-stop="{{ sk }}"]{display:flex}
#env2-stop-{{ sk }}:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__dot[data-pick~="{{ sk }}"]{transform:scale(1.5);background:var(--env2-glow);box-shadow:0 0 0 6px rgba(255,211,148,.14),0 0 18px 4px rgba(247,162,74,.34)}
#env2-stop-{{ sk }}:checked ~ {{ sc }} [data-short~="{{ sk }}"]{opacity:.4}
#env2-stop-{{ sk }}:checked ~ {{ sc }} [data-short~="{{ sk }}"] [data-short~="{{ sk }}"]{opacity:1}
#env2-stop-{{ sk }}:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__cursor{inset-inline-start:{{ cp }}%}
{% endfor -%}
#env2-stop-all:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__v{display:none}
#env2-stop-all:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__v--all{display:flex}
#env2-stop-all:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__dot[data-pick~="all"]{transform:scale(1.5);background:var(--env2-glow);box-shadow:0 0 0 6px rgba(255,211,148,.14),0 0 18px 4px rgba(247,162,74,.34)}
#env2-stop-all:checked ~ {{ sc }} .env2-coll-rail__cursor{inset-inline-start:0%}
</style>
{%- endif -%}
{%- if env2_mode == 'css_static' -%}
<style id="env2-coll-rail-css">
/* ---------- one product's dot rail (§4.2) ---------- */
.env2-coll-rail{position:relative;display:block;inline-size:100%;min-inline-size:0;
  padding-block:14px 0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300}
.env2-coll-rail__line{position:absolute;inset-inline:0;inset-block-start:8px;block-size:1px;
  background:var(--env2-hair);display:block}
.env2-coll-rail__dot{position:absolute;inset-block-start:4px;inset-inline-start:var(--env2-rail-p,0);
  margin-inline-start:-4px;inline-size:9px;block-size:9px;border-radius:999px;
  background:var(--env2-mute);display:block;
  transition:transform .25s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1),background .25s,box-shadow .25s}
/* the cursor knob — the ruler section puts this class on its own knob and the generated
   :checked ruleset moves it. It is the second and last round thing on this page (§3.1). */
.env2-coll-rail__cursor{position:absolute;inset-block-start:0;inset-inline-start:0;
  margin-inline-start:-7px;inline-size:14px;block-size:14px;border-radius:999px;
  background:var(--env2-glow);box-shadow:0 0 0 7px rgba(255,211,148,.12),0 0 22px 6px rgba(247,162,74,.30);
  transition:inset-inline-start .32s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
/* every stop's answer is in the DOM; CSS chooses. Without the generated ruleset (or with CSS off)
   the range is what shows — never nothing. */
.env2-coll-rail__v{display:none;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-block-start:12px;
  font-size:15px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--env2-ink-2)}
.env2-coll-rail__v--all{display:flex}
.env2-coll-rail__val{font-family:var(--env2-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:17px;
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--env2-ink);white-space:nowrap}
.env2-coll-rail__price{font-family:var(--env2-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:17px;
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--env2-glow);white-space:nowrap}
.env2-coll-rail__price .env2-price{--env2-price-size:17px}
.env2-coll-rail__per{font-size:14px;color:var(--env2-ink-2);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
/* 'beyond': the row dims (the ruler puts data-short on it) and the rail SAYS how far it reaches.
   Never display:none — §6.6. */
.env2-coll-rail__v[data-state="beyond"]{color:var(--env2-mute)}
.env2-coll-rail__miss{font-size:14px;color:var(--env2-ink-2)}
.env2-coll-rail__price--miss{color:var(--env2-ink-2)}
/* 'off': not measured in this unit at all — no dots, no span, only the caller's honest note. */
.env2-coll-rail--off{padding-block-start:0}
.env2-coll-rail__off{margin:0;font-size:14px;color:var(--env2-ink-2)}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .env2-coll-rail__dot,.env2-coll-rail__cursor{transition:none}
}
@media (max-width:900px){
  .env2-coll-rail__val,.env2-coll-rail__price{font-size:16px}
  .env2-coll-rail__v{font-size:14px;gap:8px}
  .env2-coll-rail__per,.env2-coll-rail__miss{font-size:13px}
}
</style>
{%- endif -%}
